.TH DENY 10 "October 2026" "1.1" "Neverdark Manual"
.SH NAME
deny \- Bar a hook or module from a region's subtree
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deny
.BR hook | module
.I name
.RI [ region ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Bar the hook or module
.I name
from running anywhere inside a region's subtree. A denied module still loads
and is still recorded in the region's set; it simply never gets to run
there. The refusal happens at dispatch time, not at load time.
.PP
The region is a bare world number (0\-65535) or the keyword \fBcosmos\fP,
under exactly the same rules as every other region selector. Without one the
command acts on your \fBdefault target region\fP (see \fBtarget\fP(10)), or
on the region you are standing in if you have set none. Regions at other
widths (see \fBgrant\fP(10)) are reached through your default; see
\fBtarget\fP(10) for the width\-and\-point form. You must rule the
region, and the region must exist: unlike \fBroom\fP there is no bootstrap
case, because there is no subtree to restrict until the region exists.
.PP
A deny is permanent for the life of the process and does not survive a
reboot, and there is no command that lifts one: plan a deny as forever, or
do not issue it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR target,loadmod,unloadmod,wall,ban (10)
.SH AUTHOR
quirinpa <quirinpa@tty.pt>
